   "reasoning_summary": "C23H22O7 has DoU 13. The 1H integrals of peaks 1-3 (10 ArH, 4:2:4) indicate two benzoates (C=O 13, 14), and peaks 11/30/12 indicate an acetate. Together these give 11 DoU and leave a C7H9O core. In the 13C data, 10 non-carbonyl sp2 signals means 8 benzoate signals plus 2 alkene CH (17, 24), so 1 DoU remains as a ring. All five sp3 carbons (25-29) lie at 57-65 ppm, so every sp3 carbon bears oxygen. Three ester O plus one ring O covering two carbons fits only with an epoxide, which accounts for the 57-61 ppm carbons and the 3.98 CH. The low 60-65 ppm carbons favour primary CH2O-esters over secondary CHOR. The proposed structure is an acyclic epoxy-butenyl framework carrying two CH2OBz groups and one CH2OAc. Regiochemistry and stereochemistry are uncertain without coupling data."
